<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0, viewport-fit=cover">
  <title>Returning to Aqua | Aquiplex</title>
  <link rel="icon" href="/logo/favicon.ico" sizes="any">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/platform.css">
  <!--
    This page is a FALLBACK ONLY. In normal operation, Android's verified App
    Link (com.aquiplex.aqua, autoVerify="true", exact path /auth/native/return)
    intercepts this URL before the browser ever renders it. Landing here means
    either App Link verification failed (check
    https://aquiplex.com/.well-known/assetlinks.json) or this was opened on a
    device without the app.

    The one-time code in this URL's query string is deliberately never
    rendered into the page body below — see docs/OAUTH_NATIVE_HANDOFF.md.
  -->
</head>
<body class="px-page">

  <main class="px-error-wrap">
    <h1>Returning to Aqua</h1>
    <p><%= message %></p>
    <div class="px-btn-row center">
      <a href="/aqua" class="px-btn px-btn-primary">Open Aqua</a>
    </div>
  </main>

<script src="/js/sw-cleanup.js" defer></script>
</body>
</html>
